                <pb facs="0392" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 803/11–12.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chinese Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-31"><hi rendition="#italic">January 31,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 84, of the 21st instant, giving a list of Chinese officials
                    specially authorized by the Chinese Government to issue to Chinese of the exempt
                    class coming to the United States from other countries than China the
                    certificate prescribed by section 6 of the act of July 5, 1884.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to say that a copy of your note has been sent to the
                    Secretary of Commerce and Labor, for his information.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
